steps.message:
This is platform app-link association, not an in-app route change. For Android, the activity declaration needs an HTTPS intent filter for the host and order path:

```csharp
[IntentFilter(
    new[] { Android.Content.Intent.ActionView },
    Categories = new[]
    {
        Android.Content.Intent.CategoryDefault,
        Android.Content.Intent.CategoryBrowsable
    },
    DataScheme = "https",
    DataHost = "example.com",
    DataPathPrefix = "/orders")]
public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
}
```

The site must serve `https://example.com/.well-known/assetlinks.json` with the real Android package name and signing-certificate SHA-256 fingerprint:

```json
[{
  "relation": ["delegate_permission/common.handle_all_urls"],
  "target": {
    "namespace": "android_app",
    "package_name": "com.example.shop",
    "sha256_cert_fingerprints": ["AA:BB:...:FF"]
  }
}]
```

For iOS, the signed app entitlement must contain `applinks:example.com` under `com.apple.developer.associated-domains`. The site must also serve `https://example.com/.well-known/apple-app-site-association` as JSON, without a filename extension or redirect:

```json
{
  "applinks": {
    "details": [{
      "appIDs": ["TEAMID.com.example.shop"],
      "components": [{ "/": "/orders/*" }]
    }]
  }
}
```

Replace the placeholder package, fingerprint, team, and bundle identifiers with the signed production values, then test the HTTPS URL on installed release-signed builds. No Shell hierarchy registration is part of this setup, and no files were changed during this read-only answer.
